the file

the buffer keeps one fact about the file: its sum as ed last read or
wrote it — `ed/1-buffer/08-save.go:/sha256/`. s writes only over that
file. text another writer put there stays until R has read it, and
then u brings the buffer back over it, so an overwrite is R u s: what
it replaces has been on screen. rejected, acme's second Put, s s: a
confirm is one more state, and it writes over text no one has seen.
the sum is of the bytes, not the time, so a rewrite with the same text
is no change and two writes inside one clock tick are two.
